# Time to first byte by region

Three distributions side by side, from raw observations rather than
pre-computed summaries. The whiskers are Tukey's, so the one point drawn beyond
the amer whisker is an outlier by a stated rule and not by eye.

```mdv box
title: Time to first byte
x: region
y: ms
whisker: tukey
outliers: true
format: table
---
region |  ms
amer   |  78
amer   |  84
amer   |  89
amer   |  92
amer   |  96
amer   | 101
amer   | 108
amer   | 214
emea   |  96
emea   | 102
emea   | 107
emea   | 111
emea   | 115
emea   | 119
emea   | 126
emea   | 134
apac   | 142
apac   | 151
apac   | 158
apac   | 164
apac   | 170
apac   | 177
apac   | 186
apac   | 198
```
